 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same list is also offered in a machine-readable form; that machine-readable list is a supported surface as of `REQ-VET-003`, no longer an unrequested artifact.
+
+Either surface — the directory page or the machine-readable list — can be narrowed to a single specialty. Given a specialty, the surface shows only the veterinarians who hold it, matched against the whole specialty name and disregarding letter case rather than by prefix. On the page, pagination applies to the narrowed list. A specialty that no veterinarian holds returns the ordinary page or document with an empty veterinarian list, not an error. An empty or blank specialty behaves as though none were given, the same rule owner search follows. With no specialty at all, both surfaces behave exactly as they did before this requirement `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the directory page is narrowed to it, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the machine-readable list is narrowed to it, then it returns only those veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either surface is narrowed to it, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a value that is a prefix of a specialty but not the whole name, when either surface is narrowed to it, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either surface is narrowed to it, then the request succeeds and the veterinarian list is empty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or whitespace-only specialty, when either surface is requested, then the result is identical to requesting it with no specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty, when either surface is requested, then it behaves exactly as it did before this requirement.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. Matching is on the whole specialty name, case aside; a value that is only a prefix of a specialty name matches nothing.
+3. A specialty held by no veterinarian returns an empty list successfully, not an error.
+4. An empty or whitespace-only specialty is treated as no specialty, exactly as an empty owner search is.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
